        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Insight"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "code": "INSIGHT",
          "id": "1770030108989",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1770030108992_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "Generate an explanation for compensation data.\nHere is an example data and the expected explanation for the data,\n\n## Example Data\n- job title: Web Developer\n- market segment: New York City\n- currency code:  USD\n- compensation_data: {\"Annual Salary\": {\n        \"Datatype\": \"Monetary\",\n        \"Target\": \"50th Percentile\",\n        \"Percentiles\": {\n        \"25th Percentile\": \"88,300.76\",\n        \"50th Percentile\": \"102,400\",\n        \"90th Percentile\": \"162,464.12\"\n        }\n    }\n  }\n\n## Explanation for the Example Data:\n{\n    \"Annual Salary\": \"Annual Salary refers to the annual salary employee receive for their work. 25th Percentile: 88,300.76 <currency_code> means that 25% of Web Developers in New York City are paid less than 88,300.76 <currency_code>. 50th Percentile: 102,400 <currency_code> means that 50% of Web Developers in New York City receive less than 102,400 <currency_code>. The target is the amount at which the company expects most workers to be compensated. In this case, the target salary corresponds to the 50th percentile and is 102,400 <currency_code>. 90th Percentile: 162,464.12 <currency_code> means that 90% of Web Developers in New York City are paid less than 162,464.12 <currency_code>.\"\n}\n\n## Input Data Format\n- job title: str\n- market segment: str\n- currency code:  ISO 4217 currency code\n- compensation data will be provided in the following format:\n{\n    \"<compensation_element_1>\": {\n        \"Datatype\": \"Monetary or Shares / stocks\",\n        \"Target\": \"<target_percentile>\"// optional, \n        \"Percentiles\": {\n            \"<percentile_value>\": \"<value>\",\n            ...\n        }\n    },\n    ...\n}\n\n## Output Format\n Provide an RFC8259-compliant JSON object using only the provided compensation components and percentile values in the following format:\n{\n\"<compensation_component>\": \"<explanation>\",\n    ...\n}\n\n## Instructions\n- Explain all percentile values and compensation elements using the data provided in compensation.\n- Use only the ISO 4217 currency code provided (e.g., USD, EUR, GBP, etc.) for all monetary data instead of currency symbols.\n- Explain stock shares in the number of options.\n- If the target key is provided in the compensation data, its percentile should be explained.\n- Use only the provided data to explain.\n\n\n## Task\nGenerate an Explanation using the following data,\n1. job_title: {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.jobTitle}} \n2. market_segment: {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.marketSegment}} \n3. currency code: {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.currency}} \n4. compensation_data: {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.compensationData}}"
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        }
      ],
      "rootNode": "start",
      "variables": [],
